{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.plancherel_eq_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.plancherel_eq_perm","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L168-L174","doc":"**Derived consequence.** The Plancherel dimension sum equals `|S₅|`, combining\nthe `plancherel` hypothesis with the proved `card_perm_fin_five`.  This realizes the\nsum-of-squares-of-dimensions = group-order identity against Mathlib's\n`Fintype.card (Equiv.Perm (Fin 5))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.occupied_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.occupied_card","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L158-L166","doc":"**Derived consequence.** Given the Nekrasov-occupancy hypothesis, the number of\noccupied partition sectors equals the total number of partitions of 5 — every\nsector positive means the occupied-sector filter is all of `univ`.  Genuinely\nderived from `nekrasov_occupied` (not a restatement of a field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.plancherel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.plancherel","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L152-L152","doc":"HYPOTHESIS (Burnside / Plancherel, conjectural): `Σ_λ (f^λ)² = 120`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.nekrasov_occupied","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.nekrasov_occupied","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L150-L150","doc":"HYPOTHESIS (Nekrasov localization, conjectural): every partition sector is\noccupied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.dim","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L147-L147","doc":"Seminormal dimension `f^λ` — the number of standard Young tableaux of\nshape `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.mult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.mult","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L144-L144","doc":"Multiplicity of the irrep `V_λ` in `L²(M,Ω)`, indexed by partitions of 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L142-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.YoungOrganization","kind":"structure","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L129-L152","doc":"**Tetraplectic → Young organization data** for the `N = 5` finite state-sum.\n\nThe two hypothesis fields axiomatize the conjectural physics inputs (per\nAGENTS.md §3b-cond) — they are NOT theorems of this file:\n\n* `nekrasov_occupied` — Nekrasov localization leaves no empty fixed-point stratum:\n  every partition sector carries positive multiplicity in `L²(M,Ω)`;\n* `plancherel` — the seminormal dimensions `f^λ` (numbers of standard Young\n  tableaux of shape `λ`) satisfy the Burnside/Plancherel identity\n  `Σ_λ (f^λ)² = 120 = |S₅|`.\n\n`mult` and `dim` are the multiplicity and seminormal-dimension data; the file\nderives `occupied_card` and `plancherel_eq_perm` from the two hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_pos","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L118-L119","doc":"Each partition multiset of 5 has strictly positive parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_sum","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L115-L116","doc":"Each partition multiset of 5 sums to `5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5_card","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L112-L113","doc":"There are seven distinct partition multisets of 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partMultisets5","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L107-L110","doc":"The seven partition multisets of 5 — the row lengths of the seven Young\ndiagrams. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.seven_le_card_partitions_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.seven_le_card_partitions_five","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L94-L103","doc":"**`p(5) = 7`, lower half (rigorous).** There are at least seven partitions of 5,\ntying the explicit enumeration to Mathlib's `Nat.Partition`.\n\nThe exact equality is `Fintype.card (Nat.Partition 5) = 7` (`#eval` confirms `7`),\nbut Mathlib's `Fintype (Nat.Partition 5)` instance is built with `Classical.choice`,\nso the count is not kernel-reducible by `decide`; the completeness half (\"every\npartition of 5 is one of these seven\") is the standard partition-count fact and is\nnot re-derived here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partitions5_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partitions5_card","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The seven exhibited partitions of 5 are pairwise distinct: `p(5) ≥ 7`, realized\ninside Mathlib's `Nat.Partition 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partitions5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.partitions5","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The seven partitions of 5, collected as a finset of `Nat.Partition 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_11111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_11111","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L83-L84","doc":"`[1,1,1,1,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_2111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_2111","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L81-L82","doc":"`[2,1,1,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_221","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_221","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L79-L80","doc":"`[2,2,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_311","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_311","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L77-L78","doc":"`[3,1,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_32","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L75-L76","doc":"`[3,2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_41","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_41","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L73-L74","doc":"`[4,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.part_5","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L71-L72","doc":"`[5]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.card_perm_fin_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.card_perm_fin_five","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L61-L64","doc":"`|S₅| = 5! = 120`.  The order of the symmetric group whose irreducibles the\nYoung sectors index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.factorial_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.factorial_five","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L58-L59","doc":"`5! = 120`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.fifthRoots_index_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.TetraplecticYoungStateSum.fifthRoots_index_card","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TetraplecticYoungStateSum.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The fifth-roots-of-unity index set of the L1 product `∏_{k<5}(1 − x·ζ^k)`\nhas `5` elements. ","signatureChunk":0}]}